    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A republic founded in 1806 in southern and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-au-prince">Port-au-Prince</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Alexandre Pétion</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-pierre-boyer">Jean-Pierre Boyer</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Pétion</a> broke up plantations into peasant smallholdings and armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> on condition that he free the slaves.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-pierre-boyer">Boyer</a> reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, ruled all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> from 1822 to 1844 and accepted a crushing French indemnity in 1825.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Pétion</a> armed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> in 1816, the payment he asked was that Bolívar abolish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the lands he freed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

